# Test fixtures are git repositories the suite creates on first run (each
# runner does its own guarded `git init`). Committing them would make them
# gitlinks, which clone as empty directories and break every test.
skills/crap-controlled-changes/test/fixture*/.git/

# Fixture build and dependency trees, created by the language-specific runs.
skills/crap-controlled-changes/test/fixture*/vendor/
skills/crap-controlled-changes/test/fixture*/.venv/
skills/crap-controlled-changes/test/fixture*/mutants/
skills/crap-controlled-changes/test/fixture*/node_modules/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json
.DS_Store

# Local term list for scripts/check-no-private-refs.sh. Never tracked: the
# point of keeping it out of the repo is that the terms stay unpublished.
.private-terms

# Agent guidance is part of this project, so it overrides a global ignore of
# **/AGENTS.md. CLAUDE.md stays ignored: it is a symlink to this file, created
# per checkout rather than committed.
!AGENTS.md

# This repo gates itself, so its own opt-in marker has to be trackable here too,
# overriding the same kind of global ignore as AGENTS.md above (personal configs
# commonly ignore **/.crap-gated so throwaway test fixtures elsewhere do not get
# staged by accident).
!.crap-gated

# Run state this plugin writes into whatever repo it runs in: per-ticket run
# records under .claude/touchstone-runs/ and the worktrees the branch phase
# cuts. Records carry absolute paths and full review findings, so they are
# local state, not something a repo's team asked for.
.claude/

# mutmut copies the source tree here and runs pytest in it.
mutants/
